The running thread counts as alone while another thread waits on the run queue.
The timer would let its request end pass, and the other thread would wait for some other event;
a turn's request end is a count the timer lets pass only while nobody waits for the core.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: the timer lets the end of the turn's request pass
Witness: fuzz bind-turn-later

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -1045,7 +1045,7 @@ uint64_t sched_next_wake(void)
     uint64_t end = turn_request_end(core);
     if (end != COUNT_NEVER) {
         /* Alone on its own time with spare time to go on with, the turn's request changes nothing that runs as it ends. */
-        bool alone = core->payer == NULL && place_spare(own) && core->run_queue == 0 && core->spare_queue == 0;
+        bool alone = core->payer == NULL && place_spare(own) && core->spare_queue == 0;
         if (!alone && end < at) {
             at = end;
         }
